  "notes": "Agent re-read after the Code Health refactor, 2026-11-07, under the owner directive transcribed in verification/reviews/rulings/agent-rereview-after-refactor-2026-11-07.md. This record is NOT an owner signature: it attests the agent's substantive reading only. It replaces a record naming the owner as reviewer, because that record's fingerprint no longer matched; that record stays in git history. Read proxy.aws_sts_credentials, proxy.aws_web_identity_credential_exchange, proxy.gcp_kms_adapter and proxy.gcp_metadata_token_lifetime against their diffs since 2026-10-12. The STS wire codec moved from aws_sts.rs to aws_sts/sts_protocol.rs; parse_assume_role_response_at became parse_assume_role_response taking the clock instant. Comparing old and new function by function: the parse is character-identical (credentials element required, each field named when missing, empty field refused, Expiration unparseable or missing reads as UNIX_EPOCH, a stated expiry is min(stated, now + MAX_SESSION_LIFETIME)), read_capped keeps its cap, validate_region is the same predicate written as a matches!, and exchange differs only in the ureq 3 call chain and passing SystemTime::now(). The 45 other functions in aws_sts.rs, including the reuse floor, the single-flight exchange and the cool-off, are unchanged. The nine parse tests differ only in the added clock argument and one qualified constant path; every expectation is the same. In gcp_kms_keysource.rs the metadata token path changed only in the call chain, so the token lifetime handling is untouched. All 28, 6 and 15 tested symbols resolve by name. The claim holds. The two feature lanes and the mutation lane were not run. Evidence class as registered (V0).",
